{"module":"schools","voice":"male","duration":180.2,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Schools: separate, unequal and still divided","start":0.0,"end":3.96,"words":[[0.05,0.58],[0.9,1.52],[1.83,2.46],[2.46,2.72],[2.72,3.08],[3.08,3.79]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Education has always been both a target and a path to freedom.","start":4.76,"end":8.54,"words":[[4.8,5.47],[5.47,5.67],[5.67,6.07],[6.07,6.27],[6.27,6.54],[6.54,6.67],[6.67,7.01],[7.01,7.21],[7.21,7.34],[7.34,7.54],[7.54,7.68],[7.68,8.15]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Enslaved people were forbidden to read; their children built thousands of schools.","start":8.89,"end":14.26,"words":[[8.94,9.55],[9.55,9.93],[9.93,10.08],[10.08,10.61],[10.61,10.76],[10.76,11.06],[11.33,11.55],[11.55,12.16],[12.16,12.46],[12.46,13.07],[13.07,13.22],[13.22,13.67]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Forbidden to read, determined to learn","start":14.61,"end":18.0,"words":[[14.63,15.38],[15.38,15.59],[15.59,16.02],[16.39,17.25],[17.25,17.46],[17.46,17.78]]},{"el":"s0","text":"After Nat Turner's rebellion, Southern states tightened laws against teaching enslaved people to read.","start":18.7,"end":25.16,"words":[[18.75,19.05],[19.05,19.28],[19.28,19.66],[19.66,20.35],[20.61,20.99],[20.99,21.45],[21.45,21.98],[21.98,22.21],[22.21,22.67],[22.67,23.13],[23.13,23.74],[23.74,24.12],[24.12,24.27],[24.27,24.57]]},{"el":"s0","text":"After emancipation, freed people built and funded schools themselves, with help from the Freedmen's Bureau.","start":25.51,"end":33.42,"words":[[25.56,25.89],[25.89,26.95],[27.24,27.57],[27.57,27.98],[27.98,28.3],[28.3,28.55],[28.55,29.04],[29.04,29.45],[29.45,30.18],[30.47,30.71],[30.71,31.04],[31.04,31.37],[31.37,31.53],[31.53,32.18],[32.18,32.84]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Between 1912 and 1932, Black communities, Booker T. Washington and philanthropist Julius Rosenwald built nearly 5,000 “Rosenwald schools” across the South, with Black families raising much of the money.","start":33.77,"end":50.28,"words":[[33.82,34.31],[34.31,35.3],[35.3,35.54],[35.54,36.69],[36.98,37.3],[37.3,38.21],[38.49,38.82],[38.82,39.07],[39.48,40.13],[40.13,40.38],[40.38,41.36],[41.36,42.02],[42.02,42.84],[42.84,43.17],[43.17,43.58],[43.58,44.48],[44.48,45.3],[45.3,45.71],[45.71,46.12],[46.12,46.28],[46.28,46.69],[46.98,47.22],[47.22,47.55],[47.55,48.13],[48.13,48.62],[48.62,48.95],[48.95,49.11],[49.11,49.27],[49.27,49.68]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Brown, and massive resistance","start":51.18,"end":54.25,"words":[[51.25,51.88],[52.24,52.56],[52.56,53.08],[53.08,54.02]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Brown v. Board of Education (1954) ruled segregated schools unconstitutional; a year later the Court ordered desegregation “with all deliberate speed,” which many states treated as never.","start":54.95,"end":67.4,"words":[[55.0,55.36],[55.36,55.58],[55.94,56.16],[56.16,56.3],[56.3,57.03],[57.03,58.05],[58.3,58.59],[58.59,59.39],[59.39,59.76],[59.76,60.99],[61.25,61.39],[61.39,61.61],[61.61,61.97],[61.97,62.12],[62.12,62.34],[62.34,62.63],[62.63,63.57],[63.57,63.79],[63.79,63.93],[63.93,64.59],[64.59,64.95],[64.95,65.24],[65.24,65.53],[65.53,65.97],[65.97,66.41],[66.41,66.55],[66.55,66.91]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The Little Rock Nine needed federal troops in 1957; six-year-old Ruby Bridges needed federal marshals in 1960.","start":67.75,"end":76.46,"words":[[67.8,67.95],[67.95,68.32],[68.32,68.54],[68.54,68.83],[68.83,69.2],[69.2,69.71],[69.71,70.08],[70.08,70.22],[70.22,71.54],[71.8,72.68],[72.68,72.97],[72.97,73.48],[73.48,73.85],[73.85,74.36],[74.36,74.8],[74.8,74.95],[74.95,75.98]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Prince Edward County, Virginia, closed its public schools from 1959 to 1964 rather than integrate, while white students attended private “segregation academies.”","start":76.81,"end":89.07,"words":[[76.85,77.21],[77.21,77.58],[77.58,78.09],[78.34,79.0],[79.25,79.69],[79.69,79.91],[79.91,80.35],[80.35,80.71],[80.71,81.0],[81.0,82.17],[82.17,82.31],[82.31,83.4],[83.4,83.69],[83.69,83.91],[83.91,84.64],[84.9,85.19],[85.19,85.48],[85.48,86.13],[86.13,86.64],[86.64,87.15],[87.15,87.95],[87.95,88.61]]},{"el":"h2","text":"The educators who were pushed out","start":89.97,"end":92.1,"words":[[90.01,90.18],[90.18,91.02],[91.02,91.19],[91.19,91.36],[91.36,91.69],[91.69,91.95]]},{"el":"s2","text":"As schools merged, Black schools were usually closed and Black principals and teachers fired or demoted.","start":92.8,"end":99.33,"words":[[92.84,92.99],[92.99,93.35],[93.35,93.78],[94.04,94.33],[94.33,94.69],[94.69,94.83],[94.83,95.34],[95.34,95.77],[95.77,95.99],[95.99,96.27],[96.27,97.0],[97.0,97.21],[97.21,97.65],[97.65,98.01],[98.01,98.08],[98.08,98.73]]},{"el":"s2","text":"An estimated 38,000 Black teachers and administrators in 17 Southern and border states lost their jobs between 1954 and 1965.","start":99.68,"end":109.83,"words":[[99.73,99.87],[99.87,100.58],[100.58,101.65],[101.65,101.93],[101.93,102.36],[102.36,102.57],[102.57,103.56],[103.56,103.7],[103.7,104.27],[104.27,104.62],[104.62,104.84],[104.84,105.12],[105.12,105.55],[105.55,105.83],[105.83,106.04],[106.04,106.4],[106.4,106.82],[106.82,107.82],[107.82,108.03],[108.03,109.3]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Research today finds that Black students who have even one Black teacher are more likely to graduate and go to college.","start":110.18,"end":117.39,"words":[[110.23,110.68],[110.68,111.05],[111.05,111.5],[111.5,111.72],[111.72,112.02],[112.02,112.69],[112.69,112.84],[112.84,113.06],[113.06,113.36],[113.36,113.58],[113.58,113.88],[113.88,114.25],[114.25,114.33],[114.33,114.48],[114.48,114.93],[114.93,115.08],[115.08,115.67],[115.67,115.9],[115.9,116.12],[116.12,116.27],[116.27,116.79]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Busing, and the line at the city limits","start":118.29,"end":121.74,"words":[[118.35,118.93],[119.28,119.57],[119.57,119.76],[119.76,120.15],[120.15,120.35],[120.35,120.54],[120.54,120.94],[120.94,121.52]]},{"el":"s3","text":"The Supreme Court upheld busing to desegregate within a district in 1971 (Swann).","start":122.44,"end":128.26,"words":[[122.49,122.63],[122.63,123.05],[123.05,123.26],[123.26,123.68],[123.68,124.03],[124.03,124.17],[124.17,124.94],[124.94,125.29],[125.29,125.43],[125.43,125.99],[125.99,126.13],[126.13,127.32],[127.32,127.67]]},{"el":"s3","text":"But in Milliken v. Bradley (1974) it barred courts from including mostly white suburbs in Detroit's remedy, so families could avoid desegregation by moving across a district line.","start":128.61,"end":140.29,"words":[[128.66,128.87],[128.87,129.0],[129.0,129.48],[129.48,129.69],[130.03,130.43],[130.43,131.52],[131.76,131.9],[131.9,132.1],[132.1,132.37],[132.37,132.65],[132.65,133.19],[133.19,133.67],[133.67,133.94],[133.94,134.35],[134.35,134.48],[134.48,135.03],[135.03,135.5],[135.74,135.95],[135.95,136.42],[136.42,136.63],[136.63,136.97],[136.97,137.85],[137.85,138.06],[138.06,138.4],[138.4,138.74],[138.74,138.87],[138.87,139.42],[139.42,139.76]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Resegregation and funding today","start":141.19,"end":143.44,"words":[[141.25,142.22],[142.22,142.44],[142.44,142.89],[142.89,143.26]]},{"el":"s4","text":"A 2016 federal report (GAO) found the share of schools that are high-poverty and mostly Black or Hispanic grew from 2000 to 2013; researchers debate how much this reflects housing patterns versus policy choices.","start":144.14,"end":158.87,"words":[[144.18,144.33],[144.33,145.33],[145.33,145.87],[145.87,146.26],[146.26,146.49],[146.76,147.15],[147.15,147.3],[147.3,147.53],[147.53,147.69],[147.69,148.07],[148.07,148.31],[148.31,148.38],[148.38,149.08],[149.08,149.31],[149.31,149.85],[149.85,150.16],[150.16,150.24],[150.24,150.85],[150.85,151.09],[151.09,151.39],[151.39,152.09],[152.09,152.24],[152.24,153.17],[153.44,154.06],[154.06,154.52],[154.52,154.75],[154.75,155.06],[155.06,155.29],[155.29,155.91],[155.91,156.38],[156.38,156.84],[156.84,157.22],[157.22,157.69],[157.69,158.31]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Funding gaps are documented: a 2019 EdBuild analysis estimated that districts serving mostly students of color received about $23 billion less a year than mostly white districts serving the same number of students, largely because schools rely on local property taxes.","start":159.22,"end":179.33,"words":[[159.27,159.75],[159.75,160.08],[160.08,160.16],[160.16,161.13],[161.41,161.58],[161.58,162.63],[162.63,163.12],[163.12,163.76],[163.76,164.57],[164.57,164.82],[164.82,165.55],[165.55,165.95],[165.95,166.52],[166.52,167.25],[167.25,167.41],[167.41,167.73],[167.73,168.22],[168.22,168.62],[168.62,169.68],[169.68,170.16],[170.16,170.41],[170.41,170.57],[170.57,170.81],[170.81,171.05],[171.05,171.62],[171.62,171.94],[171.94,172.67],[172.67,173.08],[173.08,173.24],[173.24,173.56],[173.56,173.97],[173.97,174.13],[174.13,174.94],[175.23,175.71],[175.71,176.12],[176.12,176.52],[176.52,176.93],[176.93,177.09],[177.09,177.57],[177.57,178.14],[178.14,178.71]]}]}